  "summary_plain": "Seventy-nine printed bars, all in 3/4, counted seven, seven, eight, seven, seven, seven, six, seven, seven, seven, and nine across the eleven systems. There is no pickup and no repeat. The upper staff opens in the treble clef and the lower staff opens in the bass clef. A cautionary treble clef on the lower staff at the end of P036 takes effect at P037. A cautionary bass clef on the lower staff at the end of P052 takes effect at P053. System 8 has seven complete bars between ordinary barlines. P052 closes with a double bar and that cautionary bass clef. P053 begins with three naturals on both staves, cancelling the three sharps, and its lower-staff notes are in bass. The numeral 1 above a note in P055 is a fingering, not an ending. P079 ends with the final barline. The system 8 crop includes the hairpin, the ritard, the dynamics, and the triplet numerals.",
